<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helena Dragaš</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1372–<a href="/years/1450">1450</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Hypomone</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helena Dragaš was a Serbian noblewoman, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-dragas">Konstantin Dragaš</a>, who in 1392 married the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-palaiologos">Manuel II Palaiologos</a>. She was the mother of the last two Byzantine emperors, John VIII and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI</a>, who used the surname Dragases after her family. She became a nun under the name Hypomone and is venerated as a saint by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helena-dragas.jpg" alt="Helena Dragaš" width="254" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, Byzantine period art. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Helena_Dragas_crop.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
